---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PERSON_REF } from '../data/person';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import tank from '../assets/garden/tank.jpg';
import cross from '../assets/garden/cross.jpg';
import shelf from '../assets/garden/shelf.jpg';

const shots = [
  { img: tank, alt: 'A rainforest tank a year after sealing, moss spread across the soil' },
  { img: cross, alt: 'The jar cut open: drainage, soil, moss and roots in cross-section' },
  { img: shelf, alt: 'My terrariums: every saved jar on a lit shelf, each still growing' },
];

const jsonLdApp = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebApplication',
  name: 'Glass Jar Garden',
  url: 'https://glassjar.garden/',
  applicationCategory: 'SimulationApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'Any (web browser)',
  browserRequirements: 'Requires a browser with WebGL',
  description: 'A terrarium simulator in the browser: build a jar layer by layer, plant real species, seal it and watch it live day by day.',
  author: PERSON_REF,
  offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
};
const jsonLd = [jsonLdApp, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://www.arbazsiddiqui.me/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Projects", "item": "https://www.arbazsiddiqui.me/projects/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Glass Jar Garden", "item": "https://www.arbazsiddiqui.me/glass-jar-garden/"}]}];
---

<Base
  title="Glass Jar Garden: a terrarium simulator"
  description="A terrarium simulator in the browser. Build a jar layer by layer, plant real species, seal it and watch it live: a water cycle, moss, growth and mould, day by day."
  ogImage="/og/glass-jar-garden.png"
  ogImageAlt="Glass Jar Garden, a terrarium simulator."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="narrow section">
    <p class="kicker">Free, in the browser</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Glass Jar Garden</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Build a terrarium, seal it, and watch it live. Pour the layers, plant
      real species, add a cleanup crew, then let the days run: the water
      cycles, moss creeps, plants grow, leaves fall, and mould blooms when
      something is off.
    </p>

    <dl class="facts">
      <dt>Open it</dt><dd><a href="https://glassjar.garden/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">glassjar.garden</a> · <a href="https://glassjar.garden/starter-jars/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">26 starter jars</a> · <a href="https://glassjar.garden/guide/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the guide</a></dd>
      <dt>Catalogue</dt><dd>49 plants · 31 mosses · 10 critters · 41 soils and layers · 32 stones and woods · 10 moulds</dd>
      <dt>Simulation</dt><dd>Day by day: water, light, humidity, temperature, nutrients, growth, mould and colonies of springtails and isopods</dd>
      <dt>Checked</dt><dd>14 of 14 real jars match · every starter jar alive at 2 years on 8 seeds</dd>
      <dt>Stack</dt><dd>three.js with custom shaders, Vite, no framework · Cloudflare Pages with share links on R2</dd>
    </dl>

    <video class="banner" src="/video/glass-jar-garden.mp4" poster="/video/glass-jar-garden-poster.jpg" width="1920" height="1080" autoplay muted loop playsinline controls preload="metadata" aria-label="Glass Jar Garden launch video: building a jar, a year of growth, the simulation, care, sharing and the shelf"></video>

    <div class="shots">
      {shots.map((s) => (
        <Image src={s.img} alt={s.alt} width={640} widths={[320, 480, 640]} sizes="(max-width: 640px) 80vw, 280px" loading="lazy" />
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Building</h2>
      <p>
        Every tool works like the real one. Soil pours from a scoop and piles
        up, the ground is shaped with a brush, moss is pressed down in pieces,
        and water goes in by the millilitre. Round jars, bottles and cloches
        fill along their curved glass, and stones settle onto whatever is
        under them.
      </p>
      <h2>The simulation</h2>
      <p>
        Each day the jar works out where the water is, layer by layer, how
        humid the air is under the lid, how much light each plant gets, and
        what that does to its health. Rot, grey mould, drought and heat stress
        all come out of the same numbers. Before a jar is sealed it shows a
        one-year forecast, and the guide explains every mechanism with the
        numbers it runs on.
      </p>
      <h2>Living on</h2>
      <p>
        Jars keep living while you are away and catch up when you return.
        Share one as a link that always shows it as it is now, record a
        timelapse of its whole life as a video, or take photos.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-title { margin-block: 0.35rem 0.8rem; }
  .lede { margin-bottom: 1.6rem; }
  .banner { display: block; margin-bottom: 1rem; border-radius: 6px; overflow: hidden; outline: 1px solid oklch(0 0 0 / 0.08); outline-offset: -1px; }
  video.banner { width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; background: #17261d; }
  .shots { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 2.4rem; }
  .shots img { width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 6px; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .shots {
      display: flex; overflow-x: auto; scroll-snap-type: x mandatory; scrollbar-width: none;
      margin-inline: calc(-1 * clamp(1.2rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem)); padding-inline: clamp(1.2rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem);
    }
    .shots::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
    .shots img { flex: 0 0 82%; scroll-snap-align: center; }
  }
</style>
